From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:23:05 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 21/30] Plutonium: recordings encode in a hidden page of
 Plutonium's browser; visible counts desktop-shown tabs

The encoder page came from T3's downloaded headless shell, which NixOS cannot
run, so preview_recording_start always failed. In Plutonium the helper now opens
a hidden page in its own browser for it. A browser the host cannot run now says
so, with NixOS's message. preview_status/preview_open's visible reads whether a
Plutonium shell shows the tab, and preview_open waits a moment for the panel it
asked for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
